           The OpenSSL RSA Key Encapsulation Mechanism only currently supports
           the following operation

           "RSASVE"
               The encapsulate function simply generates a secret using random
               bytes  and  then  encrypts  the secret using the RSA public key
               (with no  padding).   The  decapsulate  function  recovers  the
               secret using the RSA private key.

